{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "30", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "45", "S": "02"}}, "news": [{"title": "SC stays issuance of work order till Aug 13 in Bandra, Worli cluster redevelopment projects", "para": "The Supreme Court has temporarily halted work orders for cluster redevelopment projects.  These projects involve 132 acres in Bandra Reclamation and Worli areas.  Housing societies had challenged the government's decision to redevelop these lands.  The apex court will hear the matter again on August 13.  Until then, no work orders for the redevelopment will be issued.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/supreme-court-halts-work-orders-for-mumbais-redevelopment-projects-until-august-13/132726658?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-833578/132726658.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "RWA moves NGT against SEIAA stand on Amaltash environmental clearance in Gurugram", "para": "The National Green Tribunal is hearing a challenge to Haryana's environmental clearance for a Gurugram project.  Amaltash Residential Welfare Association has four weeks to file objections to a compliance report.  SEIAA granted clearance despite recommendations for a fresh traffic impact assessment.  A committee found traffic management relied on internal roads through residential areas.  The tribunal will next hear the matter on October sixteenth.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/ngt-hears-appeal-against-seiaa-on-amaltash-project-environmental-concerns-in-gurugram/132726610?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-342808/132726610.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Tamil Nadu registration dept to classify streets into three categories based on electricity connections", "para": "Tamil Nadu's registration department is correcting market value guideline anomalies. Streets will now be classified based on commercial electricity connections. This aims to reduce the gap between guideline and actual market values. Inconsistencies in valuations of roads and adjoining areas will be reviewed. Manpower shortages may affect the implementation of these important changes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/tamil-nadus-streets-to-be-classified-into-commercial-mixed-use-and-residential-as-registration-department-takes-action/132726542?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1826041/132726542.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}